 :least_sure
 ["The depth measure is conservative: peak container depth PLUS a cumulative prefix count that is never discharged, so 65 flat #_ forms would refuse at 65 though the reader never recurses that deep. Over-refusing is a typed refusal; under-refusing is a StackOverflowError. A closed request measures 2, and a 63-deep request is witnessed as accepted into the request contract."
  "The oracle pins the small stack to a 512 KiB THREAD rather than launching the test JVM with -Xss512k, so it is deterministic inside the gate's shared JVM. It does not prove behaviour at the gate JVM's default stack -- which is larger, i.e. weaker pressure."
  "The bound value 64 is a judgement from the request shape's own depth (2), not a measurement of where the reader overflows (256..2048 at 512 KiB, and it moves with stack size -- which is why the bound must not be derived from it)."]

 :disagreements
